      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "PURPOSE",
          "content": "Describe community nurses' experiences regarding the meaning and promotion of healthy aging in northeastern Thailand."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "METHOD",
          "content": "Data were collected through five focus group interviews with 36 community nurses in northeastern Thailand. Latent content analysis was conducted to analyze the data."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "FINDINGS",
          "content": "Healthy aging was characterized by the interconnection of older persons, older persons' family members, and the community. Healthy aging was associated with two themes: \"being strong\" and \"being a supporter and feeling supported.\" The nurses' experiences in promoting healthy aging were described by the themes \"providing health assessment,\" \"sharing knowledge,\" and \"having limited resources.\""
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "content": "The findings of this study provide a deeper understanding of the meaning of healthy aging from a holistic viewpoint. Community nurses must pay attention to older persons and their surroundings when planning how to promote healthy aging. Person-centeredness should be applied in practice to promote healthy aging. The current findings contribute useful information that should help policy makers develop healthy aging strategies in Thailand."
        }
      ]},
